ingested from agent statements - was already captured and ignored.

DESIGN DECISIONS
- 52-week year. The tenancy span is measured exclusively, so a full year
  accrues 52 x weekly rather than 52.14. Annual rent is conventionally
  52 x weekly; an inclusive count would inflate every full-year accrual.
  This matches the behaviour the page already had.
- null vs 0. No payment records means UNKNOWN, not "no rent received".
  Conflating them would report a property with no data as having earned
  nothing.
- Divergence thresholds 5% AND $500, both required. A missing month is
  ~8% of a year (triggers); rent straddling 30 June is ~2% (does not).
  The dollar floor stops a large percentage on a trivial amount - e.g. a
  tenancy running a few days - from raising a pointless warning.
  Divergence is symmetric: unexpectedly high receipts flag too.
- Thresholds exported so the UI can explain them rather than hardcoding
  numbers in copy.

